WEBVTT

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.570
I've struggled with this enough already.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.610
If you're a man...

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.650
you've got to know when it's time to make a decision.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.200
Thank you, Shigeno.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.370
I'm praying from the bottom of my heart that you can fulfill the dream of playing in the Majors...

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.120
that was too far away for me to reach.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.090
Gibson Jr!

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:37.470
My stomach hurts!

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.260
<i>He's</i> going to the Majors?

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.430
Don't make me laugh.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:44.730
How could a third-rate pitcher like him go to the Majors?

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:49.940
Not only a third-rate father, but also a third-rate friend.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.440
If I eat sitting next to losers,

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.320
I'll become a loser as well!

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.320
Wait up, dammit!

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.320
Shigeno!

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:00.830
Stop with this nonsense!

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.790
What kind of grudge do you have against me that lets you insult my dad, and now my friend!?

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:08.250
If it wasn't just before the game, I would beat you up!

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.250
I've got grudges...

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.800
Mountains of them.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.470
To you and your old man as well!

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.750
<i>The finals of the playoffs...</i>

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.460
<i>The Championship Series...</i>

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.960
<i>They've finally begun...</i>

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.170
<i>The team that wins their best of seven series becomes the Triple A Champion.</i>

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:21.430
<i>Most will bet that the Falcons will win...</i>

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:23.760
Hey!

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.510
Don't let the countryside punks from Memphis get out of here alive!

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:30.270
Show them the cowboy spirit of Oklahoma!

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:31.600
Hey, hey!

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.350
Beat them up! {The rest of it is hardly audible.}

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:36.440
<i>I guess this is to be expected when they're playing an away game...</i>

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.320
<i>It doesn't matter, I'll cheer for you alone then!</i>

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.700
<i>If you'll get to pitch, that is. {e.g., if he will get to pitch}</i>

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.880
Okay, let's go!

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.960
Put your spirits into it!

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.380
Everyone!

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.010
Fight!

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:12.100
Don't you only cosplay when we play at home?

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.310
Don't call it cosplay.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.610
It's a finals game!

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.650
It doesn't matter whether you're the home team or the visitors!{old line: Home or visitor doesn't matter!}

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.410
<i>Then how about making a bet?</i>

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:26.820
<i>A bet?</i>

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:32.000
<i>If you strike me out even once in this series,</i>

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.330
<i>then I will go to Japan...</i>

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:37.540
<i>and put my hands together and
 apologize in front of your old man's grave!</i>

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.300
<i>But in exchange...</i>

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.970
<i>If I hit just one home run off your pitches,</i>

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.470
<i>then you will get out of America immediately!</i>

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.680
<i>I'll show you, Junior!</i>

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:55.140
<i>I'll definitely make you kneel down in front of my dad's grave!</i>

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.940
Now hitting, number 2: Kelloge!

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:00.940
Play ball!

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:07.910
We're counting on you, Gasly, it's enough if you just strike him out! {Kohn: This one is hard to hear, but it's not important anyway}

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:05.200
<i>So the pitcher is Gasly, who has lead them to 18 wins this season.</i>

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.280
<i>This won't be easy for the Bats.</i>

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:14.540
Strike out!

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:20.880
Out!

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:26.510
Out!

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:30.050
This is bad.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:32.890
We won't be getting any easy points in this situation.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.140
Nice pitching!

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.310
That's a given, isn't it?

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:38.230
The Bats are no match for us.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:44.940
Now hitting, number 12: Morrow! {"moroo", some kind of name :P}

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.400
Play!

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:48.780
<i>We're counting on you, Wilson!</i>

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:52.200
<i>Hold out for as long as you can until it's Shigeno's turn!</i>

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.330
Strike out!

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.210
Okay!

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.250
Yeah!

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:08.470
Out!

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:10.090
All right!

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.470
<i>Wilson is in good form today!</i>

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:16.060
<i>His pitches are solid, and his breaking balls have a good edge.</i>

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:21.650
Now hitting, number 1: Joe Gibson Jr!

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.670
<i>The left batter's box!?</i>

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:43.960
<i>He's... a switch hitter?</i>

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.960
<i>He's... a switch hitter?</i>

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:47.170
Play!

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.720
<i>We have to be extra careful here, Wilson. Be cautious.</i>

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:57.100
Ball.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:02.100
<i>Okay, that's the way!</i>

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:04.570
<i>Don't throw even one stray ball.</i>

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.280
Ball! Ball two!

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:12.160
What is he doing? Is he planning to walk him!?

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:14.830
Even if they do that, I won't complain.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:17.250
There's a big difference in skill between him and the next batter, Boyd. {In skill}

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:23.130
<i>He really won't swing at the balls.</i>

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:24.790
Don't screw around!

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:27.050
Challenge him, you damn chicken!

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:30.840
<i>I won't throw any bad pitches today!</i>

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:32.970
<i>Throw it low and away!</i>

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.180
<i>All right!</i>

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:35.970
<i>A good course...</i>

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:55.370
You did it, Junior!

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.420
N-No way...

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:15.600
<i>Wilson's pitch wasn't bad. He threw it low and away,</i>

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:19.020
<i>yet he was able to pull it up and hit it that far!</i>

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:23.850
<i>If I hit just one home run off your pitches,</i>

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.360
<i>then you will get out of America immediately!</i>

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:29.650
<i>He's not bluffing.</i>

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:31.900
<i>That guy...</i>

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:35.280
<i>He's powered up yet another step since half a year ago!</i>

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.990
Junior really is great, don't you agree?

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.240
Y-Yeah...

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.660
<i>Even though he's not a pleasant person,</i>

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:46.130
<i>his skills are the real thing.</i>

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:52.760
Now hitting, number 5: Boyd!

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:59.760
<i>He hit my pitch that far!</i>

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:03.230
<i>Aren't my pitches any good today!?</i>

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:09.480
Ball!

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:10.730
Ball four!

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:14.450
Hey, what is he doing!?

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:16.990
It's his bad habit...

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:18.830
Tell Spencer to get ready!

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:19.830
Yes!

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:25.670
What's the matter, Wilson?

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:27.250
Your pitches weren't bad.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:28.420
Don't push yourself.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:30.340
Y-Yeah...

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:33.130
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:36.050
<i>Giving up a home run from a good pitch has disrupted his flow.</i>

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.890
<i>If I can't get him to do his best here...</i>

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:42.720
<i>we won't even make it to Shigeno's turn!</i>

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:47.940
Ball! Ball four!

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.460
Change of pitcher!

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:12.380
Wilson... didn't even last one inning...

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.010
Because Gibson Jr. hit a home run off of him...

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.840
he became a nervous wreck.

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:21.640
<i>In this first inning, there are two outs, with runners on first and second base...</i>

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:26.680
<i>If it keeps going like this, they might lose before Shigeno even gets out there.</i>

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.310
The Bats are weak!

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:32.570
This is what their starting pitcher in the first game is made of?

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:34.440
This is too easy.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:39.950
<i>What a kill-joy.</i>

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.280
<i>If this goes on...</i>

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:46.120
<i>I won't be able to knock him down. {Kohn: More literally "It won't even develop to a situation where I can knock him down"}</i>

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:50.830
Now hitting, number 8: Davenport! {"dabenpooto"... I really can't make any sense in these names... }

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:52.840
Play!

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:55.800
<i>Put a stop to this, Spencer!</i>

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.840
<i>If the point difference becomes any larger than this, it's all over!</i>

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:13.560
<i>Damn!</i>

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:18.280
Spencer!

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.740
H-How is it?

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:27.790
It's no good.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:29.870
Call the next pitcher out at once.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:31.080
The next?

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:34.540
Do you think that I have an infinite number of people prepared?

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.300
It can't be helped, can it?

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:51.890
<i>What?</i>

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:55.310
W-What is Shigeno doing?

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:59.490
Don't tell me... he's planning on pitching?

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:01.110
Boss!

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.780
Let's leave this to Shigeno.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:05.780
What?

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:09.040
N-Not only are they leading with six points, it's still only the first inning!

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:11.960
I can't let his first appearance be in a losing game!

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:15.330
It's still too early to say that we've lost this game!

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:17.630
If we get hit by Gibson Jr, who's up next...

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:19.960
Today's game... is over!

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:23.590
If we're underestimated and sandbagged from the start... {Kohn: Not certain of the meaning of "sandbagging" in baseball} {I think it means something relatively close to "lose", but since Sanders actually says "sandbag" I chose to leave it in, up to u guys though~yaHzee}

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:26.180
we won't win tomorrow or the day after!

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:27.050
True.

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:28.930
Yeah.

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:38.190
Geez... Pitch, Shigeno!

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:42.150
Yes, sir!

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:46.160
Attention please, now pitching, number 56:

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:47.780
Goro Shigeno!

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:50.500
<i>Shigeno!?</i>

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.800
<i>So you've volunteered to pitch the whole game?</i>

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:06.180
<i>I'll challenge those guts of yours on this stage.</i>

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:07.050
<i>But...</i>

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:09.890
<i>Right here and right now, both you and the Bats will meet...</i>

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:12.140
<i>the end. {Kohn: Said in "english"}</i>

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:21.360
This is a free fansub.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:21.360
Not for sale or rent.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:26.860
Shigeno, huh.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:29.330
Isn't he the guy who started a fight with us before?

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:34.120
<i>I wouldn't have imagined that he would take the field this early-</i>

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.120
Go, Junior!

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:36.290
Finish them off!

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.300
Ball!

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:45.300
95 mph!

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:47.970
153 km/h right off the bat!

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.520
<i>It seems that you've become a little better since last time.</i>

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:55.940
Ball!

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:58.150
<i>The first pitch was a low outside ball.</i>

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:00.480
<i>The second was a low inside ball.</i>

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:03.400
<i>It's not like Shigeno to run away.</i>

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:07.320
<i>You're desperately trying to get me with your inside and outside balls.</i>

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.200
Ball!

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:12.490
<i>But no matter how hard you try to scatter your pitches...</i>

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:15.080
<i>I will only swing at a strike!</i>

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:20.750
Hey, this is bad!

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:21.840
Boss!

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.420
D-Don't panic!

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.130
It's not done yet!

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.920
Right now, Shigeno's just getting started!

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:30.220
Strike!

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.850
<i>Even at 0-3, you still throw to the far corner. {No strikes, 3 balls}</i>

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:39.850
<i>You're thinking that rather than having a weak pitch be turned into a home run, it's better to walk me.</i>

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:41.900
<i>You make me sick...</i>

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.270
<i>you damn chicken!</i>

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:48.200
Strike!

00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:59.080
<i>I see.</i>

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:05.550
<i>So you're confident because you've put on that speed and those pitching skills...</i>

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:07.050
<i>However...</i>

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:11.640
<i>Do you really think that throwing only low pitches will stop me from hitting a home run off of you?</i>

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:13.970
<i>Inner high!?</i>

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:26.940
Out!

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:31.030
<i>He did it!</i>

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:33.240
All right!

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:40.000
<i>I see...</i>

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.330
<i>I made a mistake...</i>

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:43.250
<i>I completely misread him.</i>

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:46.960
<i>He wasn't afraid of giving up a home run...</i>

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:50.300
<i>He was aiming to strike me out from the start.</i>

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:55.470
You did it, Shigeno! You made him anticipate the low pitch, then completely fooled him!

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:56.510
Yeah.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:02.850
<i>But, even when his bat broke,
he still carried the ball that far...</i>

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:04.730
<i>Interesting.</i>

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:08.570
<i>That's why it's worth it to strike you out!</i>

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:18.450
Strike out!

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:24.420
Out!

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:26.290
All right!

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:31.380
Now hitting, number 10: Garrett!

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:35.800
Just get on base, Garrett!

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.850
If we take the points back a little at a time, the outcome of the game won't be definite!

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:45.900
Out!

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:48.730
Come on! Be more persistent!

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:52.570
Now hitting, number 21: Cherokee!

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:55.160
Wait up, Shigeno.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.620
You've done well.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:59.740
I'll replace you with a pinch-hitter now.

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:02.080
P-Pinch-hitter!?

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:04.500
H-Hey! Wait a second!

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:05.920
I can still pitch!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:06.580
Putting out a pinch-hitter is-

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:09.750
It's enough that you brought us through the first inning.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:11.300
However, if I let you play even more in a losing game...

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:15.380
it'll tire you out and you'll be useless for the next few games.

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:17.430
L-Losing game?

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:21.810
You just said yourself that we still don't know the outcome of this game!

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:22.980
Of course.

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:25.310
I haven't given up on this game.

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:28.310
But the important thing is that we have to win four games.

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:31.230
We can't waste all of our resources on this first game!

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:36.700
Ball! Ball four!

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:39.160
I understand, Boss.

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:42.290
I understand your reasoning.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:44.290
It's true that with a six point difference...

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.460
anyone would think like that.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:48.750
In that case...

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.000
we just have to catch up in this inning, right?

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.300
If there's a chance that we'll win...

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.260
I can still pitch, right?

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:55.680
What!?

00:17:57.090 --> 00:17:58.640
H-Hey, Shigeno!

00:17:59.100 --> 00:18:01.350
Isn't it an interesting challenge, Boss?

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:03.390
If he can't turn this game around now...

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:06.060
a big inning will be impossible. {Whatever a "big inning" is... anyone know?}

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.730
Since we've got nothing to lose, let's just go for it.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:14.440
Play!

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:16.150
He's planning to continue pitching, huh?

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:18.870
If he didn't, this would be boring!

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:22.790
Strike!

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:27.540
<i>Damn! When you reach this level, they pitch really fast!</i>

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:29.710
<i>I haven't been in the batter's box lately...</i>

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:33.420
<i>It won't be easy to hit like this.</i>

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:36.590
Ball!

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:38.380
<i>He probably...</i>

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:41.890
<i>won't use his slow change-up against a pitcher like me.</i>

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:47.310
<i>His remaining pitches should be fastballs and cutballs.</i>

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:49.230
<i>What will it be?</i>

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:53.110
<i>Since he's full of pride like me...</i>

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:56.190
<i>he won't use his winning pitch, the cutball, until he's...</i>

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:57.570
<i>cornered me!</i>

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:16.090
H-He did it!

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:18.510
You did it!

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.190
<i>You've inherited your batting from your old man too, huh?</i>

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:34.230
<i>I'm getting more and more irritated by you...</i>

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:36.280
<i>Honda Jr!</i>

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:37.900
6-2!

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:40.280
Our counterattack starts now!

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:43.700
<i>When Shigeno has said that much,</i>

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.580
<i>there's no way that I can slack off...</i>

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:48.580
<i>now!</i>

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:50.960
Yes! We got a runner!

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:53.460
We'll pressure them with all we've got in this inning!

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.760
Go, go!

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.760
All right!

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:59.800
Go around, go around!

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:05.140
Now hitting, number 8: Sanders!

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.930
If we get just one more point, Shigeno can continue pitching!

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:11.100
Just one more point!

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:13.190
<i>Well, what do you know...</i>

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:15.520
<i>These guys...</i>

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:17.610
<i>can really do it!</i>

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:22.700
All right, it got through!

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:27.700
Out!

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:34.420
I'm sorry, Shigeno.

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:35.790
I couldn't tie the score... {old line: I couldn't catch us up...}

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:37.840
It can't be helped.

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:41.550
A promise is a promise after all.

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:44.220
Boss, who will be the next pitcher?

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:45.970
Next?

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:50.430
Don't be dumb. With just a one point difference, we have to try to win this game!

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:53.850
Keep pitching, Shigeno.

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:57.900
Use that stubborn attitude of yours and win this!

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:02.030
Yes, sir!

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:10.660
Strike out!

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:12.370
All right!

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:13.540
Well done, Shigeno!

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:15.290
Nice pitching!

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.630
<i>He changed the mood of the team...</i>

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:20.960
<i>all by himself.</i>

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:24.340
All the batters were struck out in order again...

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:27.140
He's quite good, that Asian boy.

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:30.810
Ball! Ball four!

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:35.940
Good, good! No outs and a runner on base!

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:43.190
Out!

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:48.070
Now hitting, number 56: Goro Shigeno!

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:52.080
All right!

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.120
Come on!

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:02.920
Foul! Foul!

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:03.970
Foul! Foul!

00:22:03.970 --> 00:22:05.090
<i>Damn!</i>

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:07.260
<i>It was just a little bit off!</i>

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:12.060
<i>You're getting cocky. I'll show you!</i>

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:19.690
<i>I'll tie the score right here!</i>

00:24:11.800 --> 00:24:13.590
I got hit by a dead ball!

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:14.760
Dammit!

00:24:15.260 --> 00:24:17.720
I can't control my pitches because of the pain! {This line lasts way too long ~ yaHzee}

00:24:19.020 --> 00:24:20.100
In that case...

00:24:20.100 --> 00:24:22.690
I'll take you all on with just fastballs down the middle!

00:24:22.690 --> 00:24:23.980
Next time, on Major:

00:24:23.980 --> 00:24:25.820
The Pitch of Destiny.

00:24:26.320 --> 00:24:28.730
Run towards the stage of your dreams!
